   "line": 197
  },
  {
   "t": "tr",
   "id": "S0049",
   "kind": "para",
   "s": "This means that when we measure the energy we will obtain only two values, $E_1$ and $E_5$, with equal probabilities $p_1=p_2=(1/\\sqrt{2})^2$. The average energy is given by",
   "line": 197,
   "lines": [
    197
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "\n",
   "line": 197
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "\n",
   "line": 198
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "$$\\langle E \\rangle =p_1 E_1+p_2 E_2 = \\frac{1}{2}\\frac{1^2 h^2}{8mL^2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{5^2 h^2}{8mL^2}$$\n",
   "line": 199
  },
