   "t": "lit",
   "s": "\n",
   "line": 204
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "\n",
   "line": 205
  },
  {
   "t": "tr",
   "id": "S0051",
   "kind": "para",
   "s": "Consider a particle in a quantum state $\\psi$ that is a superposition of two eigenfunctions $\\phi_1$ and $\\phi_2$, with energy eigenvalues $E_1$ and $E_2$ of operator $\\hat{H}$  ($E_1 \\ne E_2$):",
   "line": 206,
   "lines": [
    206,
    206
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "\n",
   "line": 206
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "\n",
   "line": 207
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "$$\\psi = c_1\\phi_1 + c_2\\phi_2$$\n",
   "line": 208
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "\n",
   "line": 209
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "- ",
   "line": 210
  },
  {
   "t": "tr",
   "id": "S0052",
   "kind": "para",
   "s": "If one attempts to measure the energy of such a state, what will be the outcome? ",
   "line": 210,
   "lines": [
    210
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "\n",
   "line": 210
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "- ",
   "line": 211
  },
  {
   "t": "tr",
   "id": "S0053",
   "kind": "para",
   "s": "What will be the average energy and the standard deviation in energy?",
   "line": 211,
   "lines": [
    211
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": "\n",
   "line": 211
  },
  {
   "t": "lit",
   "s": ":::\n",
